</figure>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.4.1 </span>Adapter Rank</h4>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ D.4 Sampling Configurations ‣ Appendix D Ablations ‣ MOLM: Mixture of LoRA Markers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> reports the FID of watermarked images and the bit accuracy of the trained extractor for ranks {64, 32, 16, 8}. As expected, higher ranks yield stronger watermark recovery (higher bit accuracy) at the cost of slightly degraded FID, while very low ranks (8) cannot sustain reliable bit decoding.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>More Visual Examples</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tables <a href="#A5.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix E More Visual Examples ‣ MOLM: Mixture of LoRA Markers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>,  <a href="#A5.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Appendix E More Visual Examples ‣ MOLM: Mixture of LoRA Markers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>,  <a href="#A5.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ Appendix E More Visual Examples ‣ MOLM: Mixture of LoRA Markers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>,  <a href="#A5.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ Appendix E More Visual Examples ‣ MOLM: Mixture of LoRA Markers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, and <a href="#A5.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ Appendix E More Visual Examples ‣ MOLM: Mixture of LoRA Markers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> provide extended visual examples covering a different model, distortion scenarios, comparisons with existing methods, and ablations on sampling configurations and LoRA rank.</p>
</div>
